# Why this file exists — verified, not inherited.
#
# setuptools' legacy sdist default matches only `tests/test*.py`. It therefore
# omitted `tests/conftest.py` and `tests/__init__.py`. conftest.py defines all
# three fixtures the suite uses (sample_table, mapper, sample_df), so the suite
# that shipped inside the sdist could not run: installing the 0.4.1 sdist and
# running its own tests/ gave **81 passed, 33 errors**, every error being
# "fixture 'sample_table' not found" at setup.
#
# This reproduces ONLY from a clean checkout. A local `python -m build` in a
# working tree that already has `nmtc_mapper.egg-info/` picks up the stale
# SOURCES.txt, which lists conftest.py, and produces a CORRECT sdist. Since
# `*.egg-info/` is gitignored, CI never has that seed — so the artifact CI ships
# is broken while the one a maintainer builds by hand looks fine. That gap is
# why the fix has to be paired with the test-sdist job in release.yml: the
# MANIFEST.in is only what makes that job pass, and the job is what stops this
# from silently regressing again.
#
# Fourth instance of this defect in the portfolio: sbic-tracker, oz-tracker and
# cdfi-fund-tracker all hit it first. The fix was written three times and
# propagated nowhere. Packaging that is never installed from is packaging that
# is never verified.
recursive-include tests *.py

include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include LICENSE
include pyproject.toml
include setup.py

# The docs-check gate ships inside the sdist too, so the tarball carries
# everything needed to re-run the gate that certified it.
include docs-check.toml
include docs-check-denylist.txt
recursive-include tools *.py
recursive-include docs/README.expected *.txt

global-exclude *.pyc
global-exclude __pycache__/*
